WEBVTT

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.500
How horrific.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:08.880
Chiharu, the hero who would save humanity

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.340
and would be praised for all eternity
is no longer with us.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.470
What's this?

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:30.820
Hey!

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:36.280
Mukyu! The Chaotic Orbit has left 2017,

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:41.500
but among the numerous time axes,
the next connection is near 2010.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.750
I have a proposal.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.790
Next time,
I myself will assume a physical form

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.710
and carry out Chiharu's wishes.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.920
-The plan isn't over yet.
-It's not over?

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:56.970
Yes, since you're holding Shibuya
here in this era,

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.050
you can't make a time leap.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.310
However, I can.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:05.100
You don't deserve to do
such honorable duty with your rank.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.480
This is for the future of humanity
and Chiharu's honor.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:14.570
All right.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:16.360
Thank you, Mukyu.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:20.740
So, you need to have a body with flesh
and time leap to 2010, right?

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:24.710
If I wait for seven years,
then 2017 will come.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:28.960
I will observe here in 2388.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.670
And I will observe 2017.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:35.420
Then the chance of the existence
of Shibuya will be 100 percent.

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:36.430
Fine.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:40.100
But now, we need the materials
to create your body.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:47.100
Will the ancient people's sanity hold out
until we gather the materials?

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.940
And will my patience hold out as well?

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.210
<i>This is inexcusable.</i>

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:33.330
<i>Milo, you're a Balancer.</i>

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.630
<i>Your mission is to sustain a balance
for the sake of the future.</i>

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:37.880
I know that.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:39.670
It's just that...

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:40.880
<i>What?</i>

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:45.510
Is it possible that this prediction
of the future was wrong from the start?

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.350
<i>Are you referring to Daisuke Dojima?</i>

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:53.060
<i>I'll admit that several
unexpected events have occurred.</i>

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:57.230
<i>Due to this,
there's no chance now to realize </i>

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.400
<i>the future that we've predicted.</i>

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:03.990
<i>However, that doesn't change
what we must do.</i>

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.080
<i>There's no problem
with the team of String Masters, right?</i>

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.660
<i>Their relationship was already
on the verge of collapsing.</i>

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.710
<i>Keisaku Asano was the only thing
holding them together.</i>

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:17.960
<i>At present, time-space is unstable.</i>

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:20.670
<i>Unless we resolve this situation,</i>

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.130
<i>we can't reestablish predictions
of the future.</i>

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:27.260
<i>Therefore, until then,
all combat operations are suspended.</i>

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.930
<i>Since Keisaku Asano, a principal figure,
has been eliminated,</i>

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:33.060
<i>maintaining the present situation
is top priority.</i>

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:35.690
<i>We're putting the plan
of returning Shibuya on hold.</i>

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:37.770
<i>Our decision is final.</i>

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:40.570
<i>You must be kidding!</i>

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.490
Keisaku disappeared before your very eyes?

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:48.240
Are you sure? Did you look for him?

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.530
-Did you?
-Shut up!

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.200
There's no point in freaking out.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:52.750
"There's no point"?

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.870
You were all with him.
How did this happen?

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:57.000
Are you sure he wasn't there?

00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:58.960
Maybe he was shut away somewhere?

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.590
Couldn't you have expanded your search?

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:02.670
What's with you?

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.720
Are you judging what we did?

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.220
Are you blaming us
since we couldn't stop it?

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:09.140
You have no right to say that!

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:10.350
That's not what I--

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.930
Then, what did you mean?

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.270
Gai, quit being hot-tempered!
What did you say?

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.650
Daisuke, say something!

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:20.070
Quit shouting, all of you!

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:21.400
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:22.980
<i>How dare you yell at us like that?</i>

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:25.780
<i>See? Didn't I tell you?
He's nothing but a big loser!</i>

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:27.700
<i>If you all hadn't agreed, this--</i>

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:29.660
<i>How dare you bring that up, you jerk?</i>

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:32.290
<i>This is all because
you said those things, Marimari!</i>

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:34.450
<i>Why can't I worry about Keisaku?</i>

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.370
<i>-Consider our situation!
-Shut up, Mr. Perfect!</i>

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:37.870
<i>Why, you asshole!</i>

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.510
Most likely, when it happened,

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.590
Keisaku was transported
to another time-space.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.970
You mean, he made a forced time leap?

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:54.060
Why? Why would that happen to Keisaku?

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:56.940
My quantum brain sensed it then.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:06:00.650
<i>There was a quantum brain
in that Revision's body.</i>

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:04.440
He must have been caught in its time leap.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.990
So, he has been transported
to another time?

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:08.990
Then...

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:11.700
We don't know if it's the future or past,
but he's alive.

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:14.580
No. Unless he was transported
to an actual place,

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.790
he'll wander through time-space.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.670
Not to mention the fact
that Keisaku doesn't have a quantum brain.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.170
You mean, he isn't able to travel
to any time?

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:26.010
Right.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:27.550
It's likely that he's stuck

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.970
in a gap in time-space,
and his existence is scattered.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.140
Then,

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:34.390
he's dead.

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.740
<i>Are you seriously proposing this?</i>

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:52.870
Well, you see, the people on the list
were ancestors of the Revisions.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:55.490
So, if those people are dead,

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.120
isn't it possible that
the Revisions will disappear?

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:02.710
Yes, I can't deny that possibility.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:06.500
The way we were treated
when we were detained wasn't that bad.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:07.420
However...

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:08.380
Yes.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:12.680
Even if that is true, that certainly
isn't an excuse to commit murder!

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:17.140
But we have no idea
when the Revisions will counterattack.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:18.390
That's right.

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:21.230
This is no time to be idealistic.

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:24.440
Fortunately, the people rescued
from the Revisions' base

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:26.820
are being held in Seisho Academy.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:29.360
If we just light it on fire from outside--

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.570
Why the hell do you think SDS,

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:34.410
especially Asano,
put their lives on the line?

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:36.790
It was to save them!

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:38.500
Mr. Kuroiwa!

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:40.870
Chief Kuroiwa,

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:44.040
the plan you carried out
arbitrarily failed!

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.000
I know that!

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:49.670
Well, regarding this matter,

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:52.380
<i>let's take our ideas
back to our respective departments,</i>

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:55.050
<i>find common denominators,
and combine our ideas.</i>

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:56.350
<i>We can intermittently meet...</i>

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:57.600
<i>What is he talking about?</i>

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:00.270
<i>I question your qualification
to lead us, Deputy Mayor.</i>

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:02.980
<i>I am simply
a government administrator after all.</i>

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:06.440
How did it go?

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:10.240
It didn't go anywhere.
They didn't come up with any solutions.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:11.700
Those useless government officials.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:12.650
What about you?

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:15.870
Do you think you can get
those SDS kids to join us?

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:17.280
Well,

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:18.950
it's not easy.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:24.250
Do we have to keep living like this?

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:28.420
We really need to start considering
what we must do

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:32.010
<i>to survive in this time-space.</i>

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:36.640
<i>Thank you for helping
at a time like this, Lu.</i>

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:37.720
It's all right.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:39.930
When we're together,
we just end up arguing anyway.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:41.560
I'd rather get out and do something.

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:42.930
I see.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:44.390
Ms. Izumi.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:47.060
I have a message for you from Mr. Kuroiwa.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.900
Okay. Thank you for coming all this way.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:55.860
Don't move.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:59.620
Don't try anything funny. I'm serious!

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:06.920
Yes! Thank you so much!

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:11.590
I was sure I would be eventually executed.

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:14.300
Thank goodness.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.840
Chief Kuroiwa,
it appears the people need me,

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:22.060
the Prime Minister
of the Provisional Shibuya Government.

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:24.850
What do you plan on doing now?

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:27.020
In order to return to our original time,

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:30.520
the only thing we can do
is negotiate with them.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:34.320
You just behave yourself and watch.

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:36.910
Make sure you don't try
to pull any stunts.

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:40.080
Your beloved officer will be
in trouble if you do.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:41.870
<i>Lu and Ms. Izumi?</i>

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:45.580
Yes. They were taken hostage
so that Mr. Muta will be released.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:47.710
They're not hurt, are they?

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:48.880
I'm pretty sure they aren't.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:52.800
If anything happens to those two,
we won't be able to stop them.

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:54.630
"Stop them"?

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:57.550
You mean they are not only planning
to release Mr. Muta?

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:02.470
I knew it. They're planning on
reopening negotiations with the Revisions.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:03.430
You're kidding!

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:05.850
They can't be negotiated with.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:07.480
You're right.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:09.730
We have to save those two

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:11.730
and keep Muta's faction
from making any moves.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:12.940
Yes, sir.

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:13.980
Okay.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.280
Daisuke?

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:18.570
I...

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:25.040
I've always believed
in my destiny until now,

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.040
so I always thought

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.370
I wouldn't die.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:32.460
But...

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:34.000
You're afraid?

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:38.170
Daisuke! I thought
you are going to protect all of us.

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:40.640
But I couldn't protect him.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:45.100
Mr. Kuroiwa, I'll act alone
if I have to. All right?

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:50.350
Thank you, everyone.

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:51.770
Where's the other one?

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:54.230
Well, Ms. Izumi
is a police officer after all.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.440
Yes, it's better to keep her isolated.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:01.780
A String Puppet is coming, sir.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:06.870
Mr. Muta! I've brought a String Puppet.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:09.040
Give me back my sister!

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:10.330
Is that you, Gai?

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:12.960
Where's Kuroiwa?

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:14.960
I'm acting on my own.

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:23.340
Where is Ms. Izumi?

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.180
Don't worry.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:28.270
We had to put her in a dark room,
but she's all right.

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:30.440
Release both of them.

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:33.650
Gai, that's not how to negotiate.

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:35.730
And quit the negotiations
with the Revisions...

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:39.650
I told you, that's not how to negotiate.

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:42.700
Giving something equal in exchange
is basic in negotiation.

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:44.070
Are you stupid?

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:45.370
"Stupid"?

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:48.330
That's funny coming from
a jailbird ex-mayor.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:50.080
I'm not an ex-mayor!

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.620
I'm the Prime Minister
of the Provisional Shibuya Government!

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:53.750
You're no prime minister!

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:57.000
You're just in a classroom
acting like some hotshot.

00:11:57.550 --> 00:12:01.170
<i>Right. Negotiate.</i>

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:02.840
<i>You repeat it like a dumb cliché.</i>

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:06.010
<i>-You really are annoying.</i>
-He said "right" two times

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:08.060
-and "negotiate" three times.
<i>-You know what </i>

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:11.270
<i>-I've always thought? I mean, you ran for</i>
-Then, Lu's in classroom 2-C.

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:13.560
-And Izumi is in a dark room.
<i>-student council president.</i>

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:16.520
<i>-You said you'd reform the school.</i>
-Do you know where it might be, Temari?

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:19.280
<i>-You think you can do anything.</i>
-Maybe the club room or changing room.

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:21.240
-I think it's the counseling room.
<i>-I've had it.</i>

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:22.240
<i>-Besides,</i>
-Daisuke.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:25.700
<i>-you high school kids can't even vote,</i>
-It has blackout curtains

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:28.030
-and can be locked.
<i>-so how dare you negotiate with adults</i>

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:30.410
<i>-and criticize policies?</i>
-Didn't you come to save them?

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.040
<i>Children should be silent!</i>

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:34.750
<i>-Just do what us adults tell you!</i>
-I don't know anymore.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:38.040
<i>-Right, you guys? Don't you agree?</i>
-I can't believe my destiny anymore.

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:40.380
<i>-By the way, I heard</i>
-But...

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:43.590
<i>that Keisaku Asano died, didn't he?</i>

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:47.760
And he was on the returnee list too.
What a fool.

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:49.850
You're wrong!

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:53.520
There was no guarantee the people
on that list would return to our time!

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:56.940
But the possibility
of losing your life was lower.

00:12:57.400 --> 00:13:00.730
Boy, it seems you're mistaken.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:04.740
All I want to do is return as many people
as possible to our time.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:07.950
Come on, Gai. I'm sure you understand.

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:10.950
It's reckless to fight them.

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:13.120
<i>Why don't you join us instead?</i>

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.870
<i>If the negotiations succeed,
you'll be a hero, boy.</i>

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.330
<i>We won't do anything
to your sister either.</i>

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.840
<i>I don't want people to have
a pointless death like Asano's.</i>

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.760
How cruel. "A pointless death"?

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:30.760
<i>I lived my life preparing for that time
that would eventually come.</i>

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:33.730
<i>I was the only one
who could protect them all.</i>

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:37.560
<i>I could maintain my self-respect
only by believing that.</i>

00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:42.320
<i>Everyone made fun of me,
and my old friends shunned me.</i>

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:44.400
<i>But...</i>

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:49.870
<i>Keisaku. He was the only one
who stuck by my side.</i>

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:51.700
<i>But now...</i>

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:05.130
<i>Sis.</i>

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:07.590
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.560
Daisuke, I'll go.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:21.440
Let me...

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:22.820
What?

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:24.610
Let me go.

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:28.200
I'll do whatever I can.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:31.410
Who are you?

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:38.120
Ms. Izumi!

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:41.210
Hurry!

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:42.130
Lu and Gai are next.

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:43.340
Chief!

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:50.470
The Revisions!

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:53.220
I'm sorry to make you come all this way.

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:56.310
Mr. Muta, thank you for contacting me.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:58.640
There's one thing I want to check first.

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:02.560
Where are the people
you kidnapped from us?

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:03.820
Don't worry.

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:06.690
They're all in the gym,
the next building from here.

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:08.240
Good!

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:10.950
What? You there, boy.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:15.280
I believe you paid a visit
to our base the other day.

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:18.540
Thanks to you, Chiharu has died.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:21.870
One of ours died as well.

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:24.630
Kuroiwa? You're kidding.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:27.800
I never expected you to come here alone.

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:32.300
You scum have killed people mercilessly,

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:33.970
so we're never negotiating with you!

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:38.270
What the heck is going on here, Mr. Muta?

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:40.230
Hold on a second!

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:44.190
Kuroiwa! If this continues,
all the Shibuya refugees will perish!

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:45.360
Can't you understand that?

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:48.900
People need hope
if you want them to get through this!

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:49.860
But

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:52.990
nobody's life is worth sacrificing!

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:56.120
Silence! In this kind of situation,

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:58.700
it is acceptable to sacrifice some people
in order to save...

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:00.410
What?

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:02.170
Stay back!

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:03.880
Muta!

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:14.760
Nicholas, return us to our time.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:19.930
Physical damage doesn't work
on this remote communication body.

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:22.480
I know. That's why I want to negotiate.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:23.440
What?

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:27.610
Keisaku sacrificed his life
to give Shibuya a chance.

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:29.280
What we need to do now

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:33.200
is preserve the chance he gave us
for everyone else.

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:34.780
Daisuke.

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:37.120
The Revisions are suffering
from a disease, right?

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:41.330
Then give us a sample of that virus

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:43.580
and return Shibuya to our time.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:47.040
Then we'll make sure that
the pandemic doesn't occur in the future.

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:48.960
We can save humanity.

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:50.510
I see.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:54.930
That's a good proposal.

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:56.720
Nicholas.

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:07.770
However,

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:10.480
in a world without the pandemic,

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:13.690
my existence may be nullified.

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:16.280
Don't you guys want to save humanity?

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:18.780
If your unfortunate situation change--

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:21.450
<i>The only people with the right</i>

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:24.460
<i>to decide if it's unfortunate
are the people born in this era.</i>

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:27.420
<i>All that's necessary is my own existence.</i>

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:29.130
Just yourself?

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:35.260
People are quite simple.
We're the incarnation of simple desires.

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:39.100
-Are you kidding?
-Poor boy, this negotiation is over.

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:40.810
Wait! Please!

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:42.220
Nicholas,

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:46.020
we may be living in different times,
but we're still both humans.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:47.600
I want to settle this peacefully.

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:51.320
I can see you've already gone over
to the other side.

00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:55.070
The only people who can speak of ideals
are happy people.

00:17:57.360 --> 00:18:01.080
Oh, dear. What would I do? How can I...

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:09.460
-Chief!
-Damn you!

00:18:17.930 --> 00:18:22.680
What? Am I going to die?

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:32.570
Chief!

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:33.690
-Mr. Kuroiwa!
-Mr. Kuroiwa!

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:35.530
We must send him
to the hospital immediately!

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:37.280
It's pointless.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:40.160
What?

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:45.240
Listen.

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:49.670
All of you, you are the final bastion.

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:52.750
The people are becoming
restless with fear.

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:56.130
The situation is bound to get worse.

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:58.420
<i>But</i>

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:01.390
I want everyone to return.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.310
Keep fighting until that happens.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:07.930
That's the one thing I can promise...

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:11.900
Chief! That's enough! Don't talk anymore!

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:14.900
Gai, I want you

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:16.980
to lead everyone.

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:19.950
Calmly ascertain every situation.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:22.450
I know you can do it.

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:23.410
Yes, sir.

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:24.410
Lu,

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:27.080
help Izumi.

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:28.790
Mr. Kuroiwa.

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:30.580
Temari.

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:35.800
I'm sure there will be more difficulties.
Can you handle it?

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:38.010
Yes. I'll be fine.

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:39.670
Daisuke.

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:44.430
You finally pulled yourself together.

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:47.810
I'm sorry.

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:52.560
Izumi, take care of everyone.

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:56.070
Chief...

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:59.860
All of you, just like Daisuke said,

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:04.780
if you have the chance,
preserve that chance for others.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.030
That is

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:09.410
the destiny you build.

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:13.120
The destiny that is yours alone.

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:17.420
Believe in that destiny.

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:27.760
<i>This always happens to me.</i>

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:31.770
<i>I only realize that something is important
after it's gone.</i>

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:34.850
<i>Since the day
we were transported into this era,</i>

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:38.020
<i>how many lives have been lost?</i>

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:44.320
<i>Today, a huge pillar
that supported the Shibuya people</i>

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:46.530
<i>was gone.</i>

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:19.380
Who is that?

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:20.960
Is that some kind of show?

00:22:21.040 --> 00:22:23.130
That's not the Revisions, is it?

00:22:27.010 --> 00:22:29.970
I am Mukyu Isurugi of the Revisions.

00:22:30.970 --> 00:22:33.100
This is an announcement for

00:22:33.180 --> 00:22:36.600
the Revisions' ancestors, our ancestors,
who were on the returnee list.

00:22:36.770 --> 00:22:39.190
Get out of Shibuya immediately.

00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:43.270
For you other ancient people,
this is a warning.

00:22:44.110 --> 00:22:47.400
From now on,
we'll seize you indiscriminately.

00:22:50.070 --> 00:22:52.070
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
